00:03:42.551 --> 00:03:47.711
New this week is that Huang contract. It opened November 12th. It asks about a named executive

00:03:47.711 --> 00:03:53.931
coming back by calendar dates rather than naming a successor, and the December 2027 leg is the highest

00:03:53.931 --> 00:03:59.735
of the three prices just given. A published number can change the outcome it is scoring, and that is

00:03:59.735 --> 00:04:05.355
how it works in the research on performative prediction. A 2026 survey traces the idea to

00:04:05.355 --> 00:04:11.175
perdomo and co-authors in 2020, deploy a model and the environment shifts so the distribution

00:04:11.175 --> 00:04:16.935
you expected and the one you then meet no longer match. They call that shift a distribution map.

00:04:16.935 --> 00:04:22.435
Stability means the model fits the world its own use created. Optimality means it

00:04:22.435 --> 00:04:27.395
actually minimizes risk after the shift. How much you know about the map decides whether

00:04:27.395 --> 00:04:30.295
you can plan for the reaction or chase one that never comes.

00:04:31.115 --> 00:04:36.295
In the years since 2020, that literature added new solution concepts, new theory, and links

00:04:36.295 --> 00:04:42.755
to other fields. The nearest experiment here is a 2014 paper in research and politics. Our

00:04:42.755 --> 00:04:45.335
Our public opinion polls self-fulfilling prophecies.

00:04:45.775 --> 00:04:49.995
People conform to a majority and polls are how they learn what that majority is.

00:04:50.595 --> 00:04:55.835
The authors say published probabilities from prediction market contract prices and aggregated

00:04:55.835 --> 00:05:01.615
polling summaries might work the same way so a majority for a candidate or a policy could

00:05:01.615 --> 00:05:02.075
cascade.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.195
They did not trade a contract.

00:05:04.515 --> 00:05:08.835
They randomly assigned a diverse national sample to hear different levels of support for

00:05:08.835 --> 00:05:10.055
three public policies.

00:05:10.055 --> 00:05:13.855
companies, holding the policy fixed and changing only the reported support.

00:05:14.235 --> 00:05:19.415
They found that poll information changes individual attitudes, and that the size of the effect

00:05:19.415 --> 00:05:20.435
depends on the issue.

00:05:21.015 --> 00:05:25.335
If the group diverged, the published figure was an input, not only a photograph.

00:05:25.875 --> 00:05:29.075
They treat a market price as a channel that might do the same job.

00:05:29.655 --> 00:05:34.315
What they measured is poll information and attitudes, and the shift is issue-specific.

00:05:34.315 --> 00:05:40.875
A 2023 paper in ethical theory and moral practice defines a self-fulfilling prophecy as a prediction

00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:45.195
that brings about its own truth, and it names four elements that make the case.

00:05:45.735 --> 00:05:50.615
Typical examples, the authors argue, start from a mistake about how the prediction relates

00:05:50.615 --> 00:05:51.555
to its object.

00:05:52.035 --> 00:05:56.155
Because the forecast comes true, humans and machines get no error signal.

00:05:56.715 --> 00:06:01.495
Truth hides the mistake, accountability for the outcome fails, and the miscorrections

00:06:01.495 --> 00:06:02.035
feed a loop.

00:06:02.035 --> 00:06:08.155
group. They say automation can make that worse. A 2024 paper says a mis-specified distribution

00:06:08.155 --> 00:06:13.955
map can give you a poor stand-in for the true performative optimum. Its head is a distributionally

00:06:13.955 --> 00:06:19.175
robust performative optimum. Usable when the map you wrote down is not the map that actually

00:06:19.175 --> 00:06:24.495
runs, and it says that problem can be rewritten as an augmented performative prediction task.

00:06:25.055 --> 00:06:30.055
The authors claim guarantees that this robust point approximates the true optimum when

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:34.655
the nominal map and the real one differ, and experiments that look better than the ordinary

00:06:34.655 --> 00:06:40.295
approach when the misspecification is micro or macro. Chase the ordinary optimum on a

00:06:40.295 --> 00:06:45.035
wrong reaction, and you are not optimizing the outcome you thought you were. A separate

00:06:45.035 --> 00:06:48.855
2023 paper moves the same problem under inequality constraints.

00:06:49.595 --> 00:06:55.415
Earlier work, it notes, stayed unconstrained, even though transportation, finance, public policy,

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.975
and recommendation systems often face limits.

00:06:58.635 --> 00:07:03.895
It wants optimal solutions, not only stable points, and it proposes an adaptive primal

00:07:03.895 --> 00:07:05.915
dual algorithm for location families.

00:07:06.575 --> 00:07:11.255
The bounded reports is regret and constraint violations on the order of the square root of

00:07:11.255 --> 00:07:15.275
the time horizon, using the square root of T plus 2T samples.

00:07:15.915 --> 00:07:18.155
For a listener, the narrower point is enough.

